WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.075
The dangers.

2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:04.206
A manage scope on a read
client means a stolen token

3
00:00:04.206 --> 00:00:07.187
can change accounts, and
the comparison flags it.

4
00:00:07.187 --> 00:00:11.475
The workflow scope left on a standing
client lets anyone add workflows

5
00:00:11.475 --> 00:00:14.963
that call out of SailPoint, so
it lives on a client used once.

6
00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:19.131
An administrator's personal token
runs the kit as an org admin,

7
00:00:19.131 --> 00:00:21.338
so use a dedicated low-level user.

8
00:00:21.338 --> 00:00:25.276
Offset paging past ten thousand
results stops silently,

9
00:00:25.276 --> 00:00:27.287
so the code uses search-after.

10
00:00:27.287 --> 00:00:29.576
The wrong Graph cloud is refused.

11
00:00:29.576 --> 00:00:33.340
And Graph signs in with a
certificate first, not a secret.
